# Copy to .env and fill in. Nothing here is a secret in the usual sense — it
# all points at localhost — but .env is gitignored anyway so a real password
# never reaches a commit.

# --- The application under test -------------------------------------------
# The web client. The suite builds it and serves it with the project's own
# server.js, because several tests are about that server (real 404 statuses,
# CSP, brotli, immutable caching) and the Vite dev server does none of it.
WEB_PORT=4180

# The API. Deliberately NOT 8080: a backend started by hand for development
# may already hold that port, and a second one prints "Server running" while
# every request still goes to the first.
API_PORT=8081

# --- Repository locations -------------------------------------------------
# Relative to this repo. The suite starts both apps itself.
WEB_REPO=../trading_journal_web
API_REPO=../trading_journal_backend

# --- The test database ----------------------------------------------------
# A database of its own, created by `npm run db:setup`. The suite truncates
# user rows, so src/config/env.ts refuses to start against anything whose
# name is not exactly trading_journal_e2e, or any host but localhost.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/trading_journal_e2e

# --- Fixture account ------------------------------------------------------
# The admin the suite bootstraps once and then uses to mint every other test
# user over the product's own API. Must be listed in the backend's
# ADMIN_EMAILS for the role to be granted at registration.
E2E_ADMIN_EMAIL=e2e-admin@tradelogie.test
E2E_ADMIN_PASSWORD=E2eAdminPassw0rd!

# --- Options --------------------------------------------------------------
# en | tr — the language every test forces before the bundle evaluates.
# The app defaults to Turkish and never reads navigator.language.
E2E_LANG=en

# dev | build — `dev` runs Vite on its own port for a faster edit loop and
# skips the server-contract project, which has nothing to test without a
# production build.
APP_MODE=build
